yupiter - Licensing
----------------------

yupiter is free software.  You may use, copy, modify and distribute
it under your choice of one of the following three licenses:

  1. GNU General Public License, version 2 or any later version
     (SPDX identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later)
     Full text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt

  2. GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or any later
     version (SPDX identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later)
     Full text: LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt

  3. Apache License, Version 2.0 (SPDX identifier: Apache-2.0)
     Full text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

In other words: you pick the license, per use, at your option.  Every
recipient of the library may choose any of the three licenses.

Which one should I choose?
---------------------------

* Choose the Apache License 2.0 if your project must link against
  yupiter statically, for example because shared objects or DLLs
  are not an option in your environment.  The Apache License imposes
  no conditions on linking at all, static or dynamic, and grants an
  explicit patent license from the contributors.

* Choose the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPLv2.1+) if you
  link yupiter through a shared library into your own program,
  including a proprietary or closed-source program, and keep your
  program under your own license.  The obligations of the LGPL apply
  to the library itself, not to the programs that use it.

* Choose the GNU General Public License (GPLv2+) if you want your
  whole program to remain free software under the GPL family of
  licenses.

Full documentation of the licensing scheme, including the
per-condition obligations of each license and the rules for
third-party contributions, is in LICENSES/README.

Every source file of this repository carries the same multi-license
notice in its header, so a file taken out of the tree keeps its
licensing information.
